They are built from qualcomm/GenieX at tag v0.8.0 (geniex_plugin.dll) and at tag v0.9.1 (0.9.1/geniex_plugin.dll) with
the changes in geniex-castellan-memory.patch and 0.9.1/geniex-castellan-memory.patch, made by Castellan in October
2026, which change only sdk/plugins/llama_cpp: the model file is mapped rather than read into memory, the vision
encoder reserves less, loads with the first picture and is freed again after a quiet spell, and (0.9.1's build) the
processor's threads sleep while a model on the NPU or graphics works. Each change is on unless its variable is set to 0
in GenieX's environment.

They are not Qualcomm's release, and Qualcomm has not reviewed or endorsed them. They link against the llama.cpp and
GenieX libraries that GenieX installs on the PC, which are not carried here.
